                "explain": "The denominator is just the ordinary present value of all the cashflows (Module 4's technique); the numerator does the same sum but weights each term by its own timing $t$ — dividing the two gives a present-value-weighted AVERAGE time, exactly analogous to how you'd compute any other weighted average."
